DINO-CardiacSeg architecture
After domain-adaptive pretraining, we developed DINO-CardiacSeg, a segmentation model tailored to cardiac substructure segmentation, leveraging the CT-adapted DINOv3 encoder (Fig. 1b). DINO-CardiacSeg was composed of three main modules:
(1) CT-adapted ViT encoder. The input CT slice was first processed by the pretrained ViT-Base encoder, which embedded the image into a sequence of 16 × 16 non-overlapping patches and produces transformer feature representations adapted to the CT domain. (2) Hybrid CNN–Transformer adapter. In parallel, the input image was passed through a lightweight convolutional stem to generate
